# One step of the current faction's plan. Each line offers two actions.
# First-pass effects; they will be re-balanced when the 1923 events are written.

= Work for the Party Line

The party line is only words until someone does the work. What does the leadership put its weight behind this month?

- @right_unity: Approach SPD and union locals for joint action.
- @right_committees: Build joint control committees in the factories against profiteering.
- @left_hundreds: Expand the Proletarian Hundreds.
- @left_strike: Call an offensive strike wave.
- @centre_unemployed: Organise councils of the unemployed.
- @centre_unions: Build KPD fractions in the free trade unions.
- @conciliators_mass: Rebuild mass work in the unions and the factory councils.
- @conciliators_moscow: Argue the German case in Moscow, quietly.
- @root: Not this month.
- @easy_discard

@right_unity
view-if: party_line = "right"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_unity +1, workers_kpd +3×m, kf_left_dissent +4
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_unity += 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; kf_left_dissent += 4

Several SPD and union locals agree to talk, usually over the heads of their leaders. The Left calls it capitulation to the people who killed Liebknecht and Luxemburg, and they are not entirely wrong to ask what the SPD leaders will actually do in a crisis.

@right_committees
view-if: party_line = "right"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_unity +1, workers_kpd +3×m, workers_spd −1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_unity += 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; workers_spd -= 1

Joint committees against hoarding and price gouging are set up in several towns. Workers of both parties sit on them, and it is the first time in a long while that the two parties' members have acted together.

@left_hundreds
view-if: party_line = "left"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_hundreds +1, rfb_strength +20, rfb_militancy +0.02, kf_right_dissent +4
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_hundreds += 1; rfb_strength += 20; rfb_militancy += 0.02; kf_right_dissent += 4

The Proletarian Hundreds grow and drill openly, especially in Saxony and Hamburg. Their strength is real, but so is the risk: a state with an army and police will not let armed workers' units grow for ever.

@left_strike
view-if: party_line = "left"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_strikes +1, workers_kpd +4×m, workers_spd −2, kf_right_dissent +3
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_strikes += 1; workers_kpd += 4*campaign_mult; workers_spd -= 2; kf_right_dissent += 3

A wave of offensive strikes sweeps the Ruhr and central Germany. The anger is real, but a strike called without the unions' backing is easily isolated, and many SPD workers see only a party that wants them to follow it.

@centre_unemployed
view-if: party_line = "centre"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, unemployed_kpd +5×m
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; unemployed_kpd += 5*campaign_mult

Councils of the unemployed appear in the industrial towns. They give people a place to organise instead of only waiting in line, and they bind the unemployed to the party.

@centre_unions
view-if: party_line = "centre"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, workers_kpd +3×m, kf_left_dissent +2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult; kf_left_dissent += 2

Our members in the free unions form fractions and begin to win local posts. The union bureaucracy answers with expulsions, and the Left complains that this is slow, patient work.



@conciliators_mass
view-if: party_line = "conciliators"
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: -1 resources · dev: resources −1, y23_unity +1, workers_kpd +3×m
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; y23_unity += 1; workers_kpd += 3*campaign_mult

The party returns to the work that the offensive had neglected: union fractions, factory councils, joint meetings with the SPD workers. It is not exciting and it is what produces members.

@conciliators_moscow
view-if: party_line = "conciliators"
subtitle: No cost. · dev: trust +3, kf_centre_dissent +3
on-arrival: comintern_trust += 3; kf_centre_dissent += 3

Our delegates tell the Comintern's officials that the party's mass base is shrinking, in language chosen not to sound like criticism. Moscow notes the facts and the manner, and the apparatus resents it.
